cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LeanCert Python SDK: formal verification for numerical Python code"
authors:
  - family-names: "Radisic"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7612-1082"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alerad/leancert-python"
license-url: "https://github.com/alerad/leancert-python/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: "2.2.0"
date-released: "2026-08-11"
abstract: >-
  Python SDK for LeanCert: prove properties of numerical Python code for
  all inputs, powered by Lean 4. Numerical candidates from NumPy/SciPy are
  treated as untrusted inputs; accepted results carry exact rational
  certificates checked against a pinned, precompiled checker with
  content-addressed provenance (compiled_checker vs kernel_replay tiers).
  Distributed on PyPI as "leancert"; uses lean-runtime for pinned,
  pip-installable Lean environments. SDK versions through
  v0.3.2-apache-final are Apache-2.0; later versions are source-available
  under the LeanCert evaluation license (see LICENSE).
keywords:
  - "formal verification"
  - "Lean 4"
  - "Python"
  - "verified numerics"
  - "interval arithmetic"
  - "certificates"
